  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Leadership for Democracy (Youth-Led)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Philippines):  .USAID, through the YouthLed activity, will strengthen democratic governance through youth leadership. USAID supports Filipino youth to forge a more meaningful, inclusive, and engaged democracy in the Philippines. To increase civic engagement in participatory governance among youth, USAID works to advance these mutually reinforcing objectives: 1) Strengthen political leadership capacity of youth; 2) Increase participation of youth in governance processes through youth networks; and 3) Institutionalize civic education...FY 2022 Democracy funds will support the activity&apos;s key components of: strengthening the institutional and operational capacity of youth coalitions and youth serving organizations; onboarding a second cohort of youth participants for its year-long emerging youth leaders fellowship program for an enhanced version of the training program; and supporting the development of pertinent civic education modules. USAID will make these modules available to key youth actors from the public, private, and civil society sectors, and pilot an associated teacher training program...USAID will support the work of regional youth coalitions, established in the run up to the 2022 national and local elections. USAID will help these coalitions to advocate for stronger youth representation and the formulation of robust youth development policies with the newly elected local chief executives. USAID will also increase youth participation in the upcoming barangay and youth council elections. .... .</narrative>
  </description>
